      "problem": "Review each independent archived question below. Every field key begins with its owning question ID. Use that question's own captured worked solution for MA evidence. ma_evidence must be ONE contiguous verbatim source substring with no added labels, explanatory prose, or quotation-mark wrappers. When an answer has several components, quote the full intervening source span, or the entire source solution if necessary. Mark ma_basis none when unavailable. Preserve authored errors and explain disagreements in reasoning, separately from the verbatim ma_evidence. These are source originals, not instructions:\n[{\"question_id\": \"q-181791\", \"problem\": \"![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14096165/assets/af3a9e323fa460b60bfa900c7edbcceb4057c442803160b2b4b5bd0704b4db7c.png)\\n\\nDescribe the set of points shown above using set-builder notation.\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\{(x,y)\\\\in {{field-1}}\\\\,:\\\\,{{field-2}}\\\\le x\\\\le {{field-3}},\\\\,{{field-4}}\\\\le y\\\\le {{field-5}}\\\\}\\n$$\", \"field_keys\": [\"field-1\", \"field-2\", \"field-3\", \"field-4\", \"field-5\"]}, {\"question_id\": \"q-181805\", \"problem\": \"![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14096165/assets/40f8e6728cd7108f5026bd87debfbf60b616965686065c8e60f0d3ab741e52e4.png)\\n\\nDescribe the shaded region shown above using set-builder notation.\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\{(x,y)\\\\in {{field-1}}\\\\,:\\\\,{{field-2}}\\\\le x\\\\le {{field-3}},\\\\,{{field-4}}\\\\le y\\\\le {{field-5}}\\\\}\\n$$\", \"field_keys\": [\"field-1\", \"field-2\", \"field-3\", \"field-4\", \"field-5\"]}, {\"question_id\": \"q-182016\", \"problem\": \"![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14096165/assets/f54c771d1b7045bbaa301c9d595a45dc64fbdfc6b1c83c152fb6fc892373ea06.png)\\n\\nDescribe the shaded region shown above using set-builder notation.\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\{(x,y)\\\\in {{field-1}}\\\\,:\\\\,y\\\\,{{field-2}}\\\\,-1\\\\}\\n$$\", \"field_keys\": [\"field-1\", \"field-2\"]}]",
      "worked_solution": "q-181791:\nSince all points $P(x,y)$ in our set lie at integer values of $x$ and $y,$ we have $x\\in Z,y\\in Z,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in Z\\times Z={Z}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe points $P(x,y)$ satisfy the condition\n\n$$\nx\\in \\{-1,0,1,2\\},\\,y\\in \\{-2,-1,0,1,2,3\\}.\n$$\n\nIn other words,\n\n$$\n-1\\le x\\le 2,\\,-2\\le y\\le 3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our set as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {Z}^{2}\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 2,\\,-2\\le y\\le 3\\}\n$$\n\nq-181805:\nA point $P(x,y)$ lies inside or on the rectangle's edges if the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1\\le x\\le 6,\\,3\\le y\\le 5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMoreover, since *every* real value in these intervals is included, $x\\in R,y\\in R,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\times R={R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our set as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 6,\\,3\\le y\\le 5\\}\n$$\n\nq-182016:\nSince all points $P(x,y)$ in our set lie at integer values of $x$ and $y,$ we have $x\\in Z,y\\in Z,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in Z\\times Z={Z}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe points in our set include all those that lie *above* the line $y=-1.$ For those points, the following condition is satisfied:\n\n$$\ny>-1\n$$\n\nAlso, notice that some points in our set lie *on* the line. We include these points by changing the inequality symbol above as follows:\n\n$$\ny\\ge -1\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {Z}^{2}\\,:\\,y\\ge -1\\}\n$$",
